{
  "dom_id": "step-q77229",
  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "The vector $a$ is directed due north-east and $|\\,a\\,|=7$, while the vector $b$ is directed due north-west and $|\\,b\\,|=7.$ Which of the following is a unit vector that is parallel to $a+b?$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we have to find $a+b.$ According to the triangle law of addition, the resultant $a+b$ goes from the tail of $a$ to the head of $b:$   \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251721/assets/9468530a650f0bee117a4254aa87b5954c7bbbe2684d95f9db3f9961026abcb2.png)\n\nTo find the unit vector corresponding to $a+b,$ we have to divide by the magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the magnitude, first notice that we obtain a right triangle. So, we can use the Pythagorean theorem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{|a+b|}^{2} & ={|a|}^{2}+{|b|}^{2} \\\\  & ={7}^{2}+{7}^{2} \\\\  & =98\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the magnitude is\n\n$$\n|a+b|=\\sqrt{98}=7\\sqrt{2},\n$$\n\nand the corresponding unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7\\sqrt{2}}(a+b).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
